    kind: work_item  # dc73
    title: "objc: a self.<property> receiver is never typed, so 2,290 external method edges carry the 'external' sentinel and AFNetworking reaches ZERO net_recv rows (INV-linub L3; rust WI-dizag shape A is the precedent)"  # dc73
    status: todo_hard  # dc73
    priority: 2  # dc73
    parent:  # dc73
    tags:  # dc73
    - taint  # dc73
    - io_boundary  # dc73
    - analysis_quality  # dc73
    - objc  # dc73
    - receiver_typing  # dc73
    isbefore: []  # dc73
    duplicate_of: []  # dc73
    not_duplicate_of: []  # dc73
    pr_ref:  # dc73
    description: "FILED 2026-09-09 from WI-robit's census. Record:\n~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/robit_objc_09092026/RESULT.md.\n\nTHE SHAPE, isolated by contrast within the same corpus and the same run:\n\n  TYPED    [handle writeData:data]                    NSFileHandle *handle\n           reaches NSFileHandle.writeData:            a LOCAL, type written\n  UNTYPED  [self.session dataTaskWithRequest:request]  @property (readwrite,\n           reaches nothing                             nonatomic, strong)\n                                                       NSURLSession *session\n\nobjc types locals whose type is written in the declaration, and class-name\nreceivers ([NSFileManager defaultManager]). It does NOT consult an @property /\nivar declaration to type a `self.<name>` receiver, so every such call arrives\nwith the `external` sentinel in the module slot and gate_named_entry refuses it\n-- correctly, per INV-tapat: an untyped method call must not match a\nmethod-kind entry.\n\nSIZE: 2,290 external method-construct edges carry the `external` slot across\nAFNetworking / CocoaLumberjack / fmdb / Mantle, against 2,308 that ARE typed --\nso objc sits at 50.2% receiver typing on external calls and this item is the\nother half. Per repo: AFNetworking 792 untyped (52.6% typed), CocoaLumberjack\n835 (53.8%), fmdb 574 (35.6%), Mantle 89 (60.8%).\n\nCONSEQUENCE ON REAL CODE: AFNetworking -- an HTTP client -- reaches net_send\nbut ZERO net_recv rows, because its NSURLSession task creation goes through\n`self.session`. objc's catalogue has 9 net_recv rows, all NSURLSession.\n\nTHIS IS A PRECEDENTED SHAPE WITH TWO SIBLING FIXES, WHICH IS THE REASON TO\nEXPECT IT TO BE CHEAP:\n  rust    WI-dizag shape A -- self.field, closed by resolve_receiver_type\n  python  INV-mumov / WI-zamud -- self.<attr> receivers, worked twice\nRead both before designing. WI-dizag's own closure note records that shape B\n(var-rooted field chains) measured a corpus finding-delta of ZERO on spacedrive\nand shipped as a correct-by-construction ceiling; the same outcome is possible\nhere and would be an acceptable, publishable result.\n\nDO NOT ASSUME THE PAYOFF. WI-robit's census found 21.6% of objc's method rows\nalready reaching, so this item's population is the residual, not the whole\nsurface. Measure through the taint path (INV-linub 2026-09-04), not on edge\ncounts: 0012 and WI-nonad both record an emission-side win that moved zero\nfindings.\n\nFIRST TASK: confirm the mechanism at source before building. Read where objc.py\nrecords declared types today (it clearly does, for locals) and establish\nwhether @property declarations are parsed at all, or parsed and not indexed by\nreceiver name. Those are different fixes."  # dc73
    fields: {}  # dc73
- op: discuss  # 4311
  at: '2026-09-09T22:35:04Z'  # 4311
  by: agent  # 4311
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 4311
  clock: 2  # 4311
  nonce: '4311'  # 4311
  message: "FIRST TASK DONE 2026-09-09 (this item's own instruction: confirm the mechanism\nat source before building). The item asked which of TWO fixes this is --\n\"@property declarations not parsed at all, or parsed and not indexed by receiver\nname\". **NEITHER. It is a third thing, it is larger, and it is a CORRECTNESS bug\nrather than only a recall gap.**\n\nWHAT IS ACTUALLY BROKEN. `_extract_message_selector` and\n`_extract_message_receiver` share one assumption -- THE RECEIVER IS THE FIRST\n`identifier` CHILD of the `message_expression`. Each handles a NESTED receiver\n(`[[obj alloc] init]`) explicitly, by testing for a `message_expression` child.\n**Neither handles `field_expression`**, which is what `self.<prop>` parses to:\n\n    message_expression\n      [  field_expression(self.session)  identifier(dataTaskWithRequest)\n         :  identifier(request)  ]\n\nSo both functions skip past the real receiver and mis-key on the SELECTOR:\n\n  * `_extract_message_receiver` returns **\"dataTaskWithRequest\"** -- the\n    selector -- as the receiver name.\n  * `_extract_message_selector` then consumes that same identifier as the\n    \"receiver\" it must skip, and returns the **first ARGUMENT** as the selector.\n\nMEASURED ON A 12-LINE REPRO through the real analyzer, not inferred:\n\n    [self.session dataTaskWithRequest:r]  ->  objc:external:0-0:r:unresolved\n    [self.session writeData:nil]          ->  objc:NSFileHandle:0-0:nil:unresolved\n                                              receiver_type_hint='NSFileHandle'\n\nBoth slots are wrong. The name slot holds an ARGUMENT (`r`, `nil`). And the\nsecond line is a live FALSE POSITIVE: the module slot and the hint read\n`NSFileHandle` because the enclosing body declared a local named `writeData`,\nwhich collides with the selector that `_extract_message_receiver` mistook for a\nreceiver, and `_objc_receiver_type` duly looked THAT name up. The real receiver\nis `self.session`, an `NSURLSession`. A wrong module in the slot is the\nINV-fazim category error arriving from the other direction, and it can match a\ncatalogued row of the same short name.\n\nSIZE, counted from SOURCE with a stdlib-only tree-sitter scan sharing no code\nwith the analyzer: AFNetworking has 2,729 message sends, of which **429 (15.7%)\nhave a `field_expression` receiver and 379 of those are `self.<x>`**. Every one\nis mis-parsed in both slots today.\n\nSO THE FILED SIZING IS THE WRONG UNIT. \"2,290 external method edges carry the\nsentinel\" counts the recall half. It does not count the edges that carry a\nCONFIDENTLY WRONG module because a local happened to share a name with a\nselector, and those are the dangerous ones.\n\nTHE FIX IS THEREFORE TWO STAGES AND THE ORDER MATTERS:\n  1. CORRECTNESS -- teach both extractors that `field_expression` is a receiver,\n     symmetrically with the `message_expression` arm each already has. This\n     restores the selector to the name slot and REMOVES the bogus module/hint.\n     It changes existing edges, so it needs its own arm: an edge whose name slot\n     stops being an argument can start OR stop matching a row.\n  2. RECALL -- only then, type `self.<prop>` from a class-level @property/ivar\n     map. The type IS in the tree already, one node from the name\n     `_extract_property_name` extracts: `property_declaration` ->\n     `struct_declaration` -> `type_identifier` (NSURLSession) +\n     `struct_declarator` -> `pointer_declarator` -> `identifier` (session).\n     So \"parsed but the TYPE is discarded, and not indexed by receiver name\" --\n     but that is stage 2, and building it on stage 1's broken receiver would\n     have typed the wrong thing.\n\nDOING ONLY STAGE 2, AS FILED, WOULD HAVE BUILT ON A BROKEN PREMISE: the property\nmap would be keyed by a receiver name that the extractor never returns."  # 4311
- op: discuss  # b20b
  at: '2026-09-09T23:12:08Z'  # b20b
  by: agent  # b20b
  actor: jgstern_agent  # b20b
  clock: 3  # b20b
  nonce: b20b  # b20b
  message: "STAGE 1 SHIPPED 2026-09-09, PR #869, measurement 0025. **STATUS STAYS\ntodo_hard** -- this item's own headline (typing `self.<prop>`) is stage 2 and is\nuntouched. Record: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/garar_objc_09092026/.\n\nWHAT SHIPPED. `_message_receiver_node()` -- one helper answering \"which child of\na `message_expression` is the receiver\" -- replacing the three independent,\nidentical, wrong assumptions the previous entry diagnosed. Every mis-parsed\nreceiver shape is fixed at once rather than only `field_expression`: measured\nfrom source, AFNetworking's 2,729 sends are `identifier` 70.0%,\n`field_expression` 15.7%, nested `message_expression` 11.8%, and subscript /\ncall / string-literal / cast 2.4%, and only the 1st and 3rd were handled.\n\nMEASURED, four repos, both arms, blob asserted at BEGIN and END:\n\n    repo             method edges      typed        sentinel    prims via objc\n    AFNetworking     1672 -> 1801   880 -> 860    792 ->  941      12 -> 12\n    CocoaLumberjack  1808 -> 1870   973 -> 973    835 ->  897      19 -> 19\n    fmdb              891 -> 1090   317 -> 317    574 ->  773       1 ->  1\n    Mantle             227 ->  243  138 -> 138     89 ->  105       0 ->  0\n\n**787 call sites gained a correct selector; 380 of them emitted NO EDGE AT ALL\nbefore.** The old names name the mechanism: `dictionaryValueerror:` and\n`resultforKey:` are mangled concatenations of a truncated selector and the\nfollowing identifier, and `YES` is a literal argument sitting in the name slot.\n\n**The -20 typed is 20 FALSE POSITIVES REMOVED**, census-read-back to source: six\nmodule slots, `GET` 12 / `POST` 4 / `HEAD`,`PATCH`,`PUT`,`DELETE` 1 each. At\nAFHTTPSessionManagerTests.m:195, `[self.sessionManager GET:@\"/get\" parameters:…]`\nhad `GET` taken as the receiver; uppercase, so it went into the module slot as an\nObjC class that does not exist. The other three repos lost no module slots.\n\n**RECALL IS ZERO AND THAT IS STRUCTURAL, NOT A FAILURE.** Catalogue primitives\nand io-boundary chains are FLAT in all four repos. 787 correct selectors matched\nnot one extra row, because `gate_named_entry` refuses a method-kind row for an\nUNTYPED method call however correct its name is (INV-tapat/INV-maluk) and these\nsites still carry the sentinel. A correct name is NECESSARY AND NOT SUFFICIENT --\nINV-linub's L3->L4 chain exactly. This is why the item's own warning (\"DO NOT\nASSUME THE PAYOFF ... measure through the taint path\") was right, and why the\npayoff belongs to stage 2.\n\nTWO PRE-REGISTERED FALSIFIABLE PREDICTIONS HELD: primitives \"UP or flat\" (flat),\nand \"AFNetworking net_recv stays ZERO -- if it moves here my model of the fix is\nwrong\" (it stayed zero).\n\nTHE HONEST NEGATIVE. The closed-world caveat ratio got WORSE -- AFNetworking\nuntypable 798/1679 (47.5%) -> 947/1808 (52.4%), fmdb 64.4% -> 70.9% -- because\n380 previously invisible sends join the denominator while staying untyped until\nstage 2. A change that made the analysis strictly more truthful made the\ndisclosure read worse; the correct reading is that the prior estimate of the\nblind spot was too flattering by ~380 sites on this cohort.\n\nLIMIT: there is NO control repository. Every repo in the objc cohort is objc, so\nleakage outside the language cannot be shown by a within-cohort control. Weaker\nthan measurement 0024's byte-identical java/cpp controls; stated rather than\npapered over.\n\nSTAGE 2 IS NOW UNBLOCKED AND ITS TARGET IS CONCRETE: the property type is\nalready in the tree one node from the name `_extract_property_name` reads --\n`property_declaration` -> `struct_declaration` -> `type_identifier` +\n`struct_declarator` -> `pointer_declarator` -> `identifier`. Build a class-level\nmap and consult it when `_message_receiver_node` returns a `field_expression`\nrooted at `self`. AFNetworking's 9 `net_recv` rows are all NSURLSession and all\nreached through `self.session`, so that repo is the direct test."  # b20b
