- op: discuss  # 3016
  at: '2026-09-09T23:42:26Z'  # 3016
  by: agent  # 3016
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 3016
  clock: 6  # 3016
  nonce: '3016'  # 3016
  message: "STAGE 2 SHIPPED 2026-09-09, PR #870, measurement 0026. **CLOSING THIS ITEM ON\nITS FILED ROW** -- \"a self.<property> receiver is never typed\" is fixed, with\nbehavioural evidence -- **and the residual is filed, not absorbed.**\n\nBEHAVIOURAL EVIDENCE. Live on dev at 03ee437e60, a 5-line cross-file repro:\n\n    C.h:  @property (nonatomic, strong) NSFileHandle *handle;\n    C.m:  [self.handle writeData:x];\n    ->    dst  objc:NSFileHandle:0-0:writeData::unresolved\n          primitive  NSFileHandle.writeData:  |  fs_write\n\nCorpus, isolating stage 2 (BEFORE blob byte-identical to stage 1's AFTER):\n\n    repo             primitives via objc   untypable receivers\n    AFNetworking            12 -> 12       947/1808 -> 837/1810 (52.4%->46.3%)\n    CocoaLumberjack         19 -> 22      1338/2346 -> 1319/2346\n    fmdb                     1 ->  1\n    Mantle                   0 ->  0\n\nCocoaLumberjack gains three rows end to end\n(NSFileManager.contentsOfDirectoryAtPath:error:,\nNSFileManager.setAttributes:ofItemAtPath:error:,\nNSPersistentStoreCoordinator.removePersistentStore:error:). AFNetworking's\nuntypable share falls 110 sites to 46.3% -- BELOW its 47.5% from before stage 1,\nso stage 1's disclosure regression is repaid with interest.\n\n**THE HEADLINE PREDICTION WAS REFUTED AND I AM HONOURING IT AS WRITTEN.** The\npre-registration said: \"net_recv on AFNetworking goes 0 -> NON-ZERO ... if this\nstays 0 the fix does not do what the item says it does.\" IT STAYED 0. This\nitem's own filing rested on that example: \"AFNetworking -- an HTTP client --\nreaches net_send but ZERO net_recv rows, because its NSURLSession task creation\ngoes through `self.session`.\"\n\nTHE CAUSE IS ESTABLISHED, NOT GUESSED, AND IT IS A DIFFERENT COMPONENT.\ntree-sitter-objc FAILS TO PARSE AFURLSessionManager.h -- has_error True, 29\nERROR nodes, and line 96's `@property` becomes `@` plus a C function_declarator\nnamed `property`. No property_declaration node exists, so stage 2 has nothing to\nread. Counted two ways sharing no code (`@property` lines in TEXT vs nodes in\nthe TREE): **72 of 387 objc files (18.6%) carry a parse ERROR**, and 14.7% of\nAFNetworking's declared properties never become nodes -- `session` among them.\nFiled as **WI-lafom**, which also explains two knock-ons found here: `@interface\nAFURLSessionManager` produces NO class symbol, so `_project_classes` cannot\ncontain it and the emit site's `_declared not in project_classes` guard is\nsilently defeated (40 edges); and any objc census has an untrustworthy\ndenominator until something reads `has_error`.\n\nSo the mechanism WORKS (CocoaLumberjack is the demonstration) and this item's\nshowcase repository is blocked upstream. That distinction is why this closes on\nthe filed row rather than staying open: the receiver typing this item asked for\nexists and is measured; what remains is somebody else's parse.\n\nA FALSE POSITIVE IN MY OWN FIRST CUT, caught by the arm rather than by review:\n`_extract_property_type` took the FIRST `type_identifier`, and `@property\n(strong) IBOutlet UIImageView *v;` parses to TWO -- so the MACRO went into the\nmodule slot as a class (1x AFNetworking, 3x CocoaLumberjack). That is the same\nINV-fazim category error stage 1 removed 20 instances of, re-introduced by the\nstage meant to improve things. Fixed to take the LAST; arm re-run. Generic and\nprotocol-qualified types yield no bare type_identifier and correctly abstain.\n\nDIRECTION: no claim verdict moved and sanitized_flows is 0 in every repo and\narm, so the pre-registered sanitizer hazard did not materialise.\n\nLIMIT CARRIED FROM STAGE 1: there is NO control repository -- the objc cohort is\nentirely objc, so leakage outside the language cannot be shown by a within-cohort\ncontrol. Weaker than measurement 0024's byte-identical java/cpp controls.\n\nRESIDUAL FILED as **WI-koful**: three receiver shapes stay at the sentinel by\ndesign and are pinned by sentinel controls -- an INHERITED property (keyed on\nthe declaring class only; a subclass may redeclare, so the nearest declaration\nmust win), a PLAIN IVAR (not a property_declaration; cheapest of the three), and\na property on a NON-SELF receiver (the rust WI-dizag shape B that measured a\nfinding-delta of zero, so low expected payoff). None should be sized on\nAFNetworking until WI-lafom is understood."  # 3016
- op: discuss  # 6993
  at: '2026-09-10T01:29:43Z'  # 6993
  by: agent  # 6993
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 6993
  clock: 7  # 6993
  nonce: '6993'  # 6993
  message: "FOLLOW-UP 2026-09-09, not a reopen (this item is done and stays done). Its\nstage-2 HEADLINE PREDICTION -- the one measurement 0026 named as its own\nfalsifier and honoured when it failed -- is now SATISFIED, and the cause of the\nrefutation was confirmed to be the input rather than this fix.\n\n0026 predicted that typing `self.<property>` would move AFNetworking's nine\nnet_recv rows, all NSURLSession, all reached through `self.session`. net_recv\nstayed 0, and the diagnosis filed as WI-lafom was that AFURLSessionManager.h is\none of the files tree-sitter cannot parse. WI-lafom (PR #872) fixed the parse.\nRe-measured on the shipped tree, AFNetworking:\n\n    primitives reached via objc edges   12 -> 21\n    net_recv                             0 ->  2\n    net_send  4 -> 8    ipc_send  0 -> 7    ipc_recv  11 -> 14\n\nSix NSURLSession rows now reach: dataTaskWithRequest:, dataTaskWithURL:,\ndownloadTaskWithRequest:, uploadTaskWithRequest:fromData:,\nuploadTaskWithRequest:fromFile:, uploadTaskWithStreamedRequest:. These are\n`self.session` receivers typed from their @property declaration -- THIS item's\nmechanism -- reaching method-kind catalogue rows through the F3 gate.\n\nWORTH RECORDING BECAUSE THE FIRST DIAGNOSIS WAS ONLY HALF RIGHT: recovering the\nHEADER is not what did it. With the parse fix's first two rules the `session`\nproperty exists as a node and net_recv is STILL 0, because the CALLS live in\nAFURLSessionManager.m, which needed a third rule of its own. The blocker moved\nfrom the .h to the .m and had to be found a second time."  # 6993
